   "source": [
    "<a id=\"rq3\"></a>\n",
    "### 5.c. Relationship between cell type composition, PIG expression, and plaque distance\n",
    "\n",
    "- In this section we will analyze cell-type proportions and PIG expression across distance.\n",
    "- Our goal is to see if cell type composition can explain the changes in PIG expression.\n",
    "- This could reveal a potential mechanism of how the amyloid beta plaques exert their influence on the gene expression in the surrounding area.\n",
    "- In other words, we want to see if plaques change gene expression patterns by selectively killing some cells while sparing or even recruiting others.\n",
    "- Note that in this section we will use the cell type annotations provided by our teaching assistant, Ms. Tingyang Yu."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "73",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "<a id=\"rq3_cell_bin\"></a>\n",
    "#### 5.c.i. Cell composition at different distance bins"
   ]
  },
