  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "75",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "- The output of the following cell reveals the changes in cell composition with a varying distance to the nearest plaque.\n",
    "- The figure reveals that the proportion of neural cells (namely, the cortical glutamatergic \"01 IT-ET Glut\" and \"02 NP-CT-L6b Glut\" subtypes) are strongly depleted within to 30 µm radius around the plaque.\n",
    "- The subtypes \"03 OB-CR Glut\" and \"04 DG-IMN Glut\" are showing an even more drastic decrease in their population within the same region.\n",
    "- On the contrary, \"30 Astro-Epen\" glial cells as well as \"33 Vascular\" and \"34 Immune\" cell subtypes are highly enriched in the nearest distance bin.\n",
    "- This agrees well with the known mechanisms of Alzheimer's progression\n",
    "    - Existing findings reveal that amyloid plaque environment are inducing neuronal degeneration, pathological astrocytic and microglial activation, and vascular remodeling."
   ]
  },
