   "source": [
    "<a id=\"rq3_reg\"></a>\n",
    "#### 5.c.iii. Regression of PIG expression on cell type composition and plaque distance\n",
    "\n",
    "##### Mathematical formulation\n",
    "- For each PIG gene $g$, we have:\n",
    "    - $x_{ig}$ denoting the log normalized transcript count in cell $i$\n",
    "    - $d_i$ denoting the distance (µm) to the nearest plaque\n",
    "    - $t_i\\in\\mathcal{T}$ denoting the broad cell type, where\n",
    "  $$\n",
    "  \\mathcal{T} = \\{\\text{Glutamatergic},\\ \\text{GABAergic},\\ \\text{Glial},\\ \\text{Unlabeled},\\ \\text{Other}\\}.\n",
    "  $$\n",
    "- We fit an ordinary least squares (OLS) model with treatment (dummy, i.e., $k-1$ indicators relative to a baseline $t_0$) coding for $\\mathcal{T}$ and an intercept $\\beta_{0g}$ :\n",
    "  $$\n",
    "  x_{ig} \\,=\\, \\beta_{0g} \\; + \\; \\beta_{dg}\\, d_i \\; + \\; \\sum_{t\\in\\mathcal{T}\\setminus\\{t_0\\}} \\gamma_{g,t}\\, \\mathbf{1}\\{t_i=t\\} \\; + \\; \\varepsilon_{ig},\n",
    "  \\qquad \\varepsilon_{ig} \\stackrel{\\mathrm{i.i.d.}}{\\sim} \\mathcal{N}(0,\\sigma_g^2).\n",
    "  $$\n",
    "- We use the category $t_0=\\text{Unlabeled}$ as a baseline. \n",
    "- We will rely on the assumption that the unlabeled cells represent a uniform mix of all cell types.\n",
    "- Thus, each $\\gamma_{g,t}$ is the offset for type $t$ relative to the $t_0=\\text{Unlabeled}$ baseline.\n",
    "- As part of the linear regression, we test the following null hypothesis:\n",
    "  $$\n",
    "  H_0:\\ \\beta_{dg}=0 \\quad\\text{(no distance effect)}\n",
    "  $$\n",
    "- As a result of running the linear regression, we will report the train $R^2$. \n",
    "- We compute it as follows.\n",
    "- For predictions $\\hat y_i$ and ground truth $y_i$ with mean $\\bar y$, we compute\n",
    "  $$\n",
    "  R^2 \\,=\\, 1\\; -\\; \\frac{\\sum_i (y_i-\\hat y_i)^2}{\\sum_i (y_i-\\bar y)^2},\n",
    "  $$\n",
    "\n",
    "##### Results and discussion\n",
    "- For brevity, we only present the results for the Apoe gene.\n",
    "- As a result of fitting the linear model, we managed to explain 21.2% of variance of the normalized transcript count ($R^2 = 0.212$)\n",
    "- Using the F-test, we obtained the overall p-value below $2.13e-{174}$.\n",
    "- This means that we can confidently reject the joint null hypothesis $H_0$ of no significant effects.\n",
    "\n",
    "| Term | Coef (log) | p-value | Natural-scale factor | Interpretation vs Unlabeled |\n",
    "|---|---:|---:|---:|---|\n",
    "| Intercept (at d=0, Unlabeled) | 1.9074 | < 1e-300 | exp(1.9074) − 1 ≈ 5.74 transcripts | Baseline expected expression at plaque surface |\n",
    "| GABAergic | -0.4594 | < 1e-300 | exp(-0.4594) = 0.632× | 37% lower than baseline |\n",
    "| Glial | +0.4372 | < 1e-300 | exp(0.4372) = 1.549× | 55% higher than baseline |\n",
    "| Glutamatergic | -0.4676 | < 1e-300 | exp(-0.4676) = 0.627× | 37% lower than baseline |\n",
    "| Other | -0.1091 | < 1e-300 | exp(-0.1091) = 0.897× | 10% lower than baseline |\n",
    "| distance_to_plaque (per µm) | -0.0013 | < 1e-300 | exp(-0.0013) = 0.9987× per µm | Each additional µm reduces expected expression by 0.12% |\n",
    "\n",
    "- From the table above, we can see a confirmation of our previous findings:\n",
    "    - The neural cells (whether GABAergic or glutamatergic) are depleted in close proximity to the amyloid plaques.\n",
    "    - Meanwhile, the glial cells are enriched in plaque proximity."
   ]
  },
